-- title:
--   Finite part of a quasi-finite algebra over a Henselian local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a Henselian local ring, and let $S$ be a commutative $R$-algebra which is of finite type over $R$ and satisfies Mathlib's quasi-finiteness predicate `Algebra.QuasiFinite R S`. Then there exists an element $e \in S$ with the following three properties: $e$ is idempotent, $e^2 = e$; the quotient ring $S / (1-e)S$, by the ideal generated by $1-e$, is a finitely generated $R$-module; and for every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $S$ whose contraction along the structure map $R \to S$ is exactly the maximal ideal of $R$, one has $e \notin \mathfrak q$. Thus the idempotent $e$ splits off a factor $S/(1-e)S$ of $S$ that is module-finite over $R$, and the corresponding closed-and-open subset $\{e \neq 0\}$ of $\operatorname{Spec} S$ contains the whole fibre over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$. The assertion is existence only; no uniqueness of $e$ and no explicit product decomposition $S \cong S/(1-e)S \times S/eS$ is part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the algebraic form of the statement that a quasi-finite algebra over a Henselian local base splits off a finite part containing the entire special fibre (EGA IV, 18.5.11). It is used to produce, for a locally quasi-finite morphism to the spectrum of a Henselian local ring, a finite open subscheme covering the closed fibre, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isFinite_isOpenImmersion_disjoint_cover_of_locallyQuasiFinite_of_henselianLocalRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isFinite_isOpenImmersion_disjoint_cover_of_locallyQuasiFinite_of_henselianLocalRing); the proof relies on the lifting of idempotents from the closed fibre of a module-finite algebra provided by [`HenselianLocalRing.existsUnique_isIdempotentElem_mk_eq_of_moduleFinite`](thm.html#HenselianLocalRing.existsUnique_isIdempotentElem_mk_eq_of_moduleFinite).
